      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a good start, but i'm a bit worried it's a little too light on the values. \n\nsince i'm just a recent grad, i don't have a huge amount of experience to brag about, so i really need that score to be as high as possible to make up for it. i know i said don't make it look like a bot, but could you try a version that is a bit more \"value-heavy\"? maybe try to weave those specific words into my accomplishments or my vision for the role? \n\njust try to push the score a bit higher than this version did, while still trying to keep it sounding like a professional human wrote it. i really need that ATS score to be top-tier.",
      "source": "evaluator"
